        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3^2+4^2=25=5^2$. The triangle is right-angled.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2&=3^2+4^2\\\\a^2+b^2&=9+16\\\\a^2+b^2&=25\\\\h^2&=5^2\\\\h^2&=25\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a^2+b^2=h^2$, the triangle is right-angled by the converse of Pythagoras’ theorem.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
